@startuml
title Terraform v2 instance and separate cleanup lifecycle
[*] --> PENDING : persisted identity/physical intent
PENDING --> PROVISIONING : admitted Environment owner + state lock
PROVISIONING --> READY : state acknowledged, outputs/readiness valid
PROVISIONING --> FAILED : known executor/contract failure
FAILED --> PROVISIONING : one bounded known-transient retry after checks
PROVISIONING --> INTERRUPTED : process lost, outcome not proven
INTERRUPTED --> NEEDS_ATTENTION : state/provider uncertainty
INTERRUPTED --> PROVISIONING : manual stopped-owner verification, new fence
READY --> PROVISIONING : compatible non-destructive update
READY --> UNREFERENCED : last consumer removed, final commit
UNREFERENCED --> PROVISIONING : referenced again
UNREFERENCED --> DESTROYING : confirmed user/run cleanup, ownership checks
FAILED --> DESTROYING : owned run cleanup, process stopped
INTERRUPTED --> DESTROYING : operator ownership/process verification
NEEDS_ATTENTION --> DESTROYING : manually verified owned IDs, cleanup authorization
READY --> DESTROYING : test delivery detached; no consumers; explicit cleanup
DESTROYING --> DESTROYED : provider absence verified
DESTROYING --> NEEDS_ATTENTION : failed/unknown cleanup, retain remaining IDs
DESTROYED --> [*] : keep audit + terminal state
note right of NEEDS_ATTENTION
No automatic resume or orphan import (D12/D13).
Expiry alone never releases owner/lock.
No v1 adoption; no delete of preexisting/updated resources.
end note
note right of READY
ADR-017 EKS: ACTIVE alone insufficient.
Typed outputs plus API/auth/network/Ready capacity gate consumers.
Original Definition/account/region/target/state pins survive restart.
end note
@enduml
